{"availability":"available","full":"LukyVj/GSS","name":"GSS","description":"❴ ● ❵ GSS — GPU Style Sheets. A CSS-like language for 3D scenes: selectors, the cascade, nesting, keyframes and transitions, compiled into one raymarching shader for WebGPU and WebGL2. No Three.js, no meshes. Playground, VS Code extension, and a <gss-scene> tag for any page.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":58,"forks":3,"created":"2026-09-29T15:21:01Z","updated":"2026-10-09T15:56:11Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.gss-lang.dev","topics":["3d","compiler","creative-coding","css","glsl","programming-language","raymarching","sdf","shader","webgl2","webgpu","wgsl"],"demo":"https://www.gss-lang.dev/playground","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.851Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.851Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.851Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.851Z","stars":58,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Selectors, the cascade and @keyframes, compiled into a single raymarching shader.","GSS (GPU Style Sheets) is a 3D language for people who already speak CSS. You declare shapes in a @scene, style them with selectors, and the compiler turns the whole thing into GLSL and WGSL fragment shaders: signed distance fields, raymarched in WebGL2 or WebGPU. No Three.js, no meshes, no UVs.","Front-end developers already know how to describe what things look like. The moment they want to go 3D, they hit GLSL: distance functions, vectors and math, written in a way that has little to do with how they think about design. GSS is a way in: a familiar syntax to start creating in 3D today, and a readable path toward the shader underneath. It is not meant to replace GLSL."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LukyVj/GSS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9b2165598bc38027a980614d08f95ae02d35856567de21df79369d6a6804a9e8","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.966Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.966Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Selectors, the cascade and @keyframes, compiled into a single raymarching shader.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LukyVj/GSS/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9b2165598bc38027a980614d08f95ae02d35856567de21df79369d6a6804a9e8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LukyVj/GSS/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.966Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T15:56:11Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LukyVj/GSS/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:01:05.967Z","hash":"9b2165598bc38027a980614d08f95ae02d35856567de21df79369d6a6804a9e8","originalBytes":12442,"storedBytes":12442,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["scene","gss","gss-lang","hover","glsl","page","webgl2","webgpu","color","colors","cube","like","shader","css","mount","objects","sphere","time","wgsl","backend","canvas","import","keyframes","one","only","path","runtime","selectors","view","what","when","cascade","distance","each","face","gpu","gss-lang.dev","math","playground","scenes","shows","style","translate","variables","without","any","api","background","camera","compile","compiler","draws","every","file","how","keeps","light","mountasync","noise","scene.update","shapes","texture","they","url","var","webgpu.","already","animated","animation","around","asynchronous","auto","await","block","brand","build","calc","changes","code","compiled","computer","const","contour","controls","cylinder","default","describe","device","example","export","feature","filter","filters","first-child","float","fragment","frame","function","functions","gradients","group","groups","hovered","hsl","html","icon","image","images","including","inside","install","jelly","leaves","license","lights","live","logo","make","media","moment","motion","needed.","npm","object","once","opacity","other","othersource","paint","panel","patterns","